# Equality is the one operator that could have answered a description rather
# than refusing it: it reaches its own arm before the type table, and that arm
# could have called two descriptions equal. It names them instead. The page
# gets this sentence by handing the interpreter a description, so it is the
# oracle's own words and not a copy.
# The check refuses a provable box here now (the errors corpus pins that
# sentence), so the box travels through a list, where nothing can prove it.
import "std/io"

pub fn opaque v
  (push [] v)[1]!

d = io/write "a\n" >> io/write "b\n"

pub play = print "{opaque d == opaque d}"
